    "body": "I see.\r\n\r\nI didn't look at \"the rules for choosing a browsing context\" because I'm not sure whether affecting `window.open()` is reasonable. I vaguely recall weird ad networks using the window name to transfer data across the window boundary. Not sure if that's done a priori via targeting, or after the fact by setting `window.name`.",
